# configflux-jraj — write-path constraint enforcement over the session's total
# known assignment (ADR-0017 amendment 2026-08-03). One target for the whole
# group: every case shares the `write_enforcement` name infix, so the substring
# filter selects exactly these nine and nothing else. They cover the three write
# commands, both transports (CLI and C ABI), D1's precondition ordering, D3's
# partial-assignment semantics and D2's skip-on-disagreement rule, all on the
# committed `s_labeled_mus` fixture already carried by SCENARIO_COMPILE_DATA.
